        323.33
      ],
      "text": "Subject:- Recruitment to the grade of Lower Division\nClerk-Groficiency in typewriting-Question of\nrecognition of tests held under the Hindi\nTeaching Scheme.\nUnit 24-1000"
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "text",
      "order": 12,
      "poly": [
        105.91,
        360.38,
        514.67,
        360.38,
        514.67,
        582.66,
        105.91,
        582.66
      ],
      "text": "The uddersigned is directed to say that instructions were issued under this Department O.M.-No. 14020/5/79-Estt. (D) dated 20th September, 1979, to the effect that the typing test under the Hindi Teaching Scheme was not designed to test the speed of the candidates in Hindi typewriting. It cannot be recognised as equivalent to a pass in typing test in Hindi held by the Staff Selection Commission at 25 w.p.m. for the purposes of regularisation \"of the\" appointment as IDC/grant of increments. The typing test conducted under the above scheme has undergone a major change w.e.f. 23.3.1985 and the employee is now required to qualify at 25 w.p.m. A mention to this effect is also made in the certificates issued by the Department of Official Language. It has therefore been decided that w.e.f. 23.3.1985 the certificate in typewriting issued under the Hindi Teaching Scheme would be treated as equivalent to the certificate issued by the Staff Selection Commission for purposes of regularisation of IDCs, drawal rules of etc. Necessary amendments to the requirements of the may be made accordingly, whenever necessary."
    },
